(Here?s a comment I read in the code I was working on. Walk the entire collection to locate) Tj
T*
(flagged clusters. Skip it altogether when the cached, dirty-tracked flag count says there are) Tj
T*
(none \(the usual case\): nothing needs marking, so the walk is pure waste. When the count is) Tj
T*
(stale \(e.g. right after an edit\) or non-zero, we fall through to the real lookup, so stale) Tj
T*
(marks never show. Same eventually-consistent signal the ?Flags? badge relies on. One thing in) Tj
T*
(this comment caught my mind: the small parenthetical that says ?the usual case?. If that were) Tj
T*
(true, it would be important information! However, this comment is generated by the LLM model) Tj
T*
(Claude, which has no sense of what counts as the usual case in this domain. But by generating) Tj
T*
(that comment, it tricks every future reader \(both human and robot\) into believing in a property) Tj
T*
(of the system that does not exist. \(Continue reading the full article on the web.\)) Tj
